itecture\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-2\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFClements\" class=\"citation book cs1\">Clements, Alan. <i>Principles of Computer Hardware</i> (Fourth&#160;ed.). p.&#160;1. <q>Architecture describes the internal organization of a computer in an abstract way; that is, it defines the capabilities of the computer and its programming model. You can have two computers that have been constructed in different ways with different technologies but with the same architecture.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=Principles+of+Computer+Hardware&amp;rft.pages=1&amp;rft.edition=Fourth&amp;rft.aulast=Clements&amp;rft.aufirst=Alan&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComputer+architecture\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77f8cc8f9b‐q84gk\nCached time: 20260918180831\nCache expiry: 2592000\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.169 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.263 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 195/1000000\nRevision size: 1678/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 4163/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 465/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 8/100\nExpensive parser function count: 1/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4722/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.120/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 3467121/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  239.075      1 -total\n 46.72%  111.688      1 Template:Short_description\n 45.46%  108.687      1 Template:Cite_web\n 25.81%   61.71